  ('GLG 103', 'Basic and Applied Geology for Environmental, Physical and Social Sciences', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Pure and Industrial Chemistry', '200 Level', 'first', 3, 'Elective. The earth and the solar system; internal structures and physics of the earth; important minerals and major rock types; geologic time-scale and geochronology; elements of earth history; relationship between geomorphic and structural features; weathering and erosion, gullying, landslide, floods, desert advance, and environmental pollution, and their control; outlines of the geology and mineral resources of Nigeria.', '["The earth and the solar system", "Internal structures and physics of the earth", "Important minerals and major rock types", "Geologic time-scale and geochronology", "Elements of earth history", "Relationship between geomorphic and structural features", "Weathering and erosion, gullying, landslide, floods, desert advance, and environmental pollution, and their control", "Outlines of the geology and mineral resources of Nigeria"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Pure and Industrial Chemistry undergraduate programme'),
  ('STA 203', 'Statistics for Physical Sciences and Engineering I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Pure and Industrial Chemistry', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Elective. Initial steps in planning of biological experiments. Methods of data collection, presentation and analysis. Measures of central tendency and dispersion. Frequency distributions. Elementary probability. Discrete and continuous distributions: Binomial, Poisson, Normal and exponential distributions. Interval estimation.', '["Initial steps in planning of biological experiments", "Methods of data collection, presentation and analysis", "Measures of central tendency and dispersion", "Frequency distributions", "Elementary probability", "Discrete and continuous distributions: Binomial, Poisson, Normal and exponential distributions", "Interval estimation"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Pure and Industrial Chemistry undergraduate programme'),
